From 40dce0ccab1c550db713b110bc273f7659814d08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 10:43:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 077/124] net: airoha: make GDM2 the xPON data interface

Move the xPON link lifecycle and data-plane ownership to the GDM2
netdevice. The GPON and EPON control driver no longer allocates a pon%d
netdevice. Opening and closing GDM2 starts and stops the SFP/xPON
provider, and the public carrier follows the optical state.

Enable the matching GDM2 TX and CDM2 hardware-forwarding channel when a
GPON T-CONT is programmed. Build GPON QDMA descriptors from resolved GEM
Port-ID and T-CONT metadata, and keep a small service table for
CPU-originated traffic. OMCI traffic uses the same descriptor path with
T-CONT 0.

Extend the OMCI hardware callback with the referenced T-CONT entity so
that GEM Port Network CTP objects can provision the initial service
mapping. This mapping is intentionally limited to VLAN-tag metadata and
a single default service until bridge and VLAN MEs are fully resolved.

Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
